{
  "dom_id": "step-e7580",
  "name": "Example: Computing the Mean of a Data Set From the Sum",
  "problem": "Given a data set with $12$ data points and $\\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^{12} x_i = 96,$ compute $\\overline{x}.$",
  "worked_solution": "If we have a data set that consists of the points $x_1, x_2, \\ldots, x_n,$ then the mean is denoted by $\\overline{x}$ and is given by the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\overline{x} = \\dfrac{1}{n} \\sum_{i=1}^n x_i\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=12$ and $\\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^{12} x_i = 96,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\u2015}{x} & =\\frac{1}{12}\\cdot 96=8.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
